('dph-pharmacology-extra-mcq-39','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mcq','free',2239,'{"question":"Dependence may be","translation":"Dependence may be","options":["Psychological and/or physical adaptation","Only improved appetite","A change in tablet shape","No adaptation"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Dependence can be psychological, physical or both.","explanationNe":"Dependence मानसिक, शारीरिक वा दुवै हुन सक्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mcq-40','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mcq','free',2240,'{"question":"Rational medicine use means","translation":"Rational medicine use means","options":["Right medicine, patient, dose, route and duration","Any medicine for every symptom","Sharing prescriptions","Stopping when feeling better"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Rational use matches treatment to patient and clinical need.","explanationNe":"बिरामी र clinical आवश्यकताअनुसार सही औषधि, dose, route र अवधि प्रयोग गर्नु rational use हो।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-01','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2301,'{"question":"Explain pharmacokinetics and its four main processes.","answer":"It describes what the body does to a drug: absorption, distribution, metabolism and excretion (ADME).","answerNe":"यसले शरीरले औषधिमाथि गर्ने प्रक्रिया अध्ययन गर्छ: absorption, distribution, metabolism र excretion (ADME)।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-02','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2302,'{"question":"Differentiate pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics.","answer":"Pharmacokinetics describes ADME and concentration over time. Pharmacodynamics describes drug effects and mechanisms.","answerNe":"Pharmacokinetics ले ADME र concentration बताउँछ। Pharmacodynamics ले औषधिको प्रभाव र कार्यविधि बताउँछ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-03','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2303,'{"question":"Define bioavailability.","answer":"Bioavailability is the rate and extent active drug reaches systemic circulation. Route, formulation, absorption and first-pass metabolism may affect it.","answerNe":"सक्रिय औषधि systemic circulation मा पुग्ने दर र मात्रा bioavailability हो। Route, formulation, absorption र first-pass metabolism ले असर गर्छन्।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-04','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2304,'{"question":"What is first-pass metabolism?","answer":"It is metabolism in the intestinal wall and/or liver before a drug reaches systemic circulation, potentially reducing oral bioavailability.","answerNe":"Systemic circulation पुग्नुअघि आन्द्राको भित्ता वा कलेजोमा हुने metabolism first-pass metabolism हो। यसले oral bioavailability घटाउन सक्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-05','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2305,'{"question":"Define half-life and state its importance.","answer":"Half-life is the time for drug concentration or amount to decrease by 50%. It helps guide dosing intervals and time to steady state.","answerNe":"औषधिको concentration वा मात्रा ५०% घट्न लाग्ने समय half-life हो। यसले dose interval र steady state समय बुझ्न मद्दत गर्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-06','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2306,'{"question":"Differentiate agonist and antagonist.","answer":"An agonist binds and activates a receptor. An antagonist binds without activating it and blocks agonist action.","answerNe":"Agonist receptor सक्रिय बनाउँछ। Antagonist receptor मा बाँधिए पनि सक्रिय नगरी agonist को प्रभाव रोक्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-07','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2307,'{"question":"What is therapeutic index?","answer":"It compares toxic and effective dose measures and indicates relative safety. A narrow index needs careful dosing and monitoring.","answerNe":"यसले toxic र effective dose तुलना गरी सुरक्षाको संकेत दिन्छ। Narrow index मा dose र monitoring सावधानीपूर्वक गर्नुपर्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-08','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2308,'{"question":"Define adverse drug reaction.","answer":"An ADR is a harmful and unintended response at normally used doses. Examples may include rash, bleeding or severe allergy.","answerNe":"सामान्य dose मा हुने हानिकारक अनिच्छित प्रतिक्रिया ADR हो। उदाहरण rash, bleeding वा गम्भीर allergy हुन सक्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-09','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2309,'{"question":"What is pharmacovigilance?","answer":"It involves detecting, assessing, understanding and preventing adverse effects and other medicine-related problems.","answerNe":"औषधिको adverse effect तथा अन्य समस्या पत्ता लगाउने, मूल्याङ्कन गर्ने, बुझ्ने र रोक्ने गतिविधि pharmacovigilance हो।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-10','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2310,'{"question":"Differentiate tolerance and dependence.","answer":"Tolerance is reduced response after repeated exposure. Dependence is psychological and/or physical adaptation that may cause symptoms on reduction or stopping.","answerNe":"Tolerance बारम्बार प्रयोगपछि प्रतिक्रिया घट्नु हो। Dependence मानसिक वा शारीरिक अनुकूलन हो, औषधि रोक्दा लक्षण आउन सक्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-11','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2311,'{"question":"Explain loading and maintenance doses.","answer":"A loading dose rapidly reaches target concentration. A maintenance dose replaces eliminated drug to maintain therapeutic concentration.","answerNe":"Loading dose ले चाहिएको concentration छिटो प्राप्त गर्छ। Maintenance dose ले निष्कासित औषधि पूर्ति गर्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-12','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2312,'{"question":"Describe major routes of drug administration.","answer":"Routes include oral and sublingual, parenteral routes such as IV, IM and SC, and topical or inhalational routes. Selection depends on clinical need.","answerNe":"Oral, sublingual, IV, IM, SC, topical र inhalational route प्रमुख हुन्। छनोट clinical आवश्यकतामा निर्भर हुन्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-13','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2313,'{"question":"State advantages and risks of IV administration.","answer":"IV gives direct systemic entry and rapid effect. Risks include infection, dosing error and rapid toxicity.","answerNe":"IV ले सीधै रगतमा औषधि पुर्‍याउँछ। जोखिममा infection, dose error र छिटो toxicity पर्छन्।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-14','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2314,'{"question":"Explain drug interactions and their types.","answer":"One drug or substance changes another drug''s effect. Interactions may be pharmacokinetic (ADME) or pharmacodynamic (effect).","answerNe":"एउटा औषधि वा पदार्थले अर्कोको प्रभाव बदल्छ। Interaction pharmacokinetic (ADME) वा pharmacodynamic (effect) हुन सक्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-15','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2315,'{"question":"List factors that alter drug response.","answer":"Age, body size, genetics, pregnancy, kidney and liver function, disease, dose, route and interacting medicines can alter response.","answerNe":"उमेर, शरीरको आकार, genetics, गर्भावस्था, मिर्गौला/कलेजोको कार्य, रोग, dose, route र अन्य औषधिले प्रतिक्रिया बदल्छन्।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-16','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2316,'{"question":"Explain rational medicine use.","answer":"Use the appropriate medicine for the right patient, indication, dose, route and duration, with clear information and monitoring.","answerNe":"सही बिरामीका लागि उपयुक्त औषधि, indication, dose, route र अवधि प्रयोग गर्नु rational use हो।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-17','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2317,'{"question":"What should be checked before dispensing a prescription?","answer":"Check patient, medicine, strength, dosage form, dose, route, frequency, duration, allergies, interactions and clarity. Clarify uncertainty with prescriber.","answerNe":"बिरामी, औषधि, strength, dosage form, dose, route, frequency, अवधि, allergy, interaction र स्पष्टता जाँच्नुपर्छ। अस्पष्टता prescriber सँग स्पष्ट गर्नुपर्छ।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-18','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2318,'{"question":"Describe steps when a serious ADR is suspected.","answer":"Arrange urgent clinical assessment, follow emergency procedures, document details and report through the appropriate pharmacovigilance pathway.","answerNe":"तुरुन्त clinical assessment गर्ने, emergency प्रक्रिया पालना गर्ने, विवरण लेख्ने र pharmacovigilance प्रणालीमा report गर्ने।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-19','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2319,'{"question":"What is medication adherence and how can a pharmacist support it?","answer":"Adherence means following the agreed treatment plan. Explain purpose and schedule, check understanding, discuss barriers and encourage follow-up.","answerNe":"Adherence भनेको उपचार योजना पालना गर्नु हो। उद्देश्य र समय बुझाउने, बुझाइ जाँच्ने, समस्या छलफल गर्ने र follow-up प्रोत्साहन गर्ने।"}'::jsonb,true),
('dph-pharmacology-extra-mock-20','Pharmacy','Diploma in Pharmacy','mock','free',2320,'{"question":"Why monitor drugs with a narrow therapeutic index?","answer":"Small concentration changes may cause toxicity or loss of effect. Follow prescribed monitoring and adjust only under authorized clinical supervision.","answerNe":"सानो concentration परिवर्तनले toxicity वा प्रभाव घट्न सक्छ। तोकिएको monitoring गर्ने र अधिकारप्राप्त clinical supervision मा मात्र dose परिवर्तन गर्ने।"}'::jsonb,true)
